Troubleshooting Tips
Common Issues and Solutions
Issue: Pods not starting or staying in pending state

Solution: Check resource availability with kubectl describe pod <pod-name> -n traffic-routing
Issue: Routing rules not taking effect

Solution: Verify Istio proxy injection with kubectl get pods -n traffic-routing -o wide and look for 2/2 ready containers
Issue: Cannot reach services

Solution: Check service endpoints with kubectl get endpoints -n traffic-routing
Issue: Headers not being recognized

Solution: Ensure header names and values match exactly (case-sensitive)
Verification Commands
# Check all Istio configurations
kubectl get virtualservice,destinationrule -n traffic-routing

# Verify proxy configuration
kubectl exec -n traffic-routing $SLEEP_POD -c istio-proxy -- pilot-agent request GET config_dump

# Check service connectivity
kubectl exec -n traffic-routing $SLEEP_POD -c sleep -- nslookup reviews
